possible_values: []
value_names: None
value_delimiter: None
default_values: ["false"]
help_heading: Some("Global Options")
conflicts: []
set: ["global"]
help: Some("Assume no user is available to answer prompts")
long_help: Some("Assume no user is available to answer prompts.\n\nEverything JP would ask about resolves the way it does when JP runs without a terminal: the workspace and conversation pickers, the lock-timeout prompt, and a third-party plugin's approval all fail, and a tool set to ask before running runs unconfirmed.\n\nA command with no answer to fall back on fails too: `jp init`, and any removal or archive it would have to confirm.\n\nSet `JP_NONINTERACTIVE=1` to apply this to every invocation in an environment, such as a script or a CI job.\n\nThis does not change output formatting; use `--format` for that.")

