help_heading: None
conflicts: ["no_service_tier"]
set: []
help: Some("Capacity tier to request from the provider")
long_help: Some("Capacity tier to request from the provider.\n\nProviders sell more than one grade of capacity for the same model: `flex` is cheaper and slower, `priority` is faster and pricier, `standard` is the regular rate, and `off` asks for no tier at all.\n\nWhich tiers are available depends on the provider, the model, and the account; a provider that sells no equivalent refuses the query rather than falling back to a rung that costs something else. One that sells the tier but cannot serve this model with it may still fall back.\n\nApplies to this query and every later one on the conversation, because each tier is served from separate capacity and switching discards the prompt cache.")

